  "english": "24. Sunday. Tone 2 [b3]. Fifth [Sunday of Advent]. Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 2 [b3]: \"The angel of good tidings\" (Zyn avetavor) and \"Today they rejoiced\" (Aysor zvartatsan).\n\n29. Friday. Tone 8 [dk]. Fast-breaking [Eve] of the Fast of the Nativity.\n\n30. Saturday. Tone 1 [az]. Fast of the Nativity of Christ, [Feast of] Basil of Caesarea, and the others.\n\n31. Sunday. Tone 2 [ak]. Sixth [Sunday of Advent]. Fast. Patristic Hymn [Harts] Tone 6 [g3]: \"Only-begotten Son\" (Miatsin vordi). Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 2 [ak]: \"The wondrous resurrection\" (Zhrashali zyarutyun).\n\nJanuary\n\n1. Monday. Tone 3 [bch / b2]. Fasting day. Patristic Hymn [Harts] Tone 8 [dk]: \"Blessed art thou, Lord God of our fathers.\"\n\n5. Friday. Tone 7 [dch / d2]. Candlelight Vigil [Chragaluyts] of the Nativity of Christ.\n\nTHE SEVEN-DAY CYCLE OF THE ROMANS\n\nMay\n\n12. Thursday. Tone 8 [dk]. Ascension of Christ into heaven.\n\n22. Sunday. Tone 4 [a2 / ad]. Coming of the Holy Spirit [Pentecost]. Fast-breaking [Eve] of the Elias Fast.\n\n29. Sunday. Tone 1 [az]. First [Sunday]. Beginning of the Sundays of Resurrection. Patristic Hymn [Harts] Tone 1 [ay]: \"Who came for the salvation of the universe.\"\n\nJuly\n\n10. Sunday. Tone 3 [bch / b2]. Vardavar [Transfiguration]. The period of non-fasting [eating days] is four weeks. Until the Friday of the third week, look in the First Volume, and on Saturday come here, and celebrate the feast days placed herein, which are those of the Octave. But when it is a leap year, and the year-letter is 140 [TsKh], do not celebrate the Sunday here, for it was celebrated in the first letter 90 [Ts], but celebrate [the feast of] Vahan and Gordios on Monday; and in other years, as written, celebrate without doubt.\n\n30. Saturday. Tone 7 [dgch / d2]. Gregory the Theologian.\n\n31. Sunday. Tone 8 [dk]. Fourth [Sunday]. Patristic Hymn [Harts] Tone 4 [bk]: \"Who of the heavenly hosts.\" Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 8 [dk]: \"When they came\" (Yorzham ekin) and \"The angel descended\" (Ej hreshtakn).\n\nJanuary\n\n6. Thursday. Feast of the Nativity and Epiphany of Christ. The period of non-fasting [eating days] is eighteen days.\n\n15. Saturday. John the Forerunner [John the Baptist].\n\n16. Sunday. First [Sunday]. Patristic Hymn [Harts] Tone 7 [dz]: \"The dawning of the Only-begotten\" (Tsagumn miatsni).\n\n17. Monday. Peter the Patriarch, Blaise, and the others.\n\n18. Tuesday. Anton [Anthony], and Tryphon, Parsamas, and Onuphrius the hermits.\n\n20. Thursday. Theodosius the King, and the Holy Infants of Ephesus.\n\n22. Saturday. Athanasius and Cyril, Patriarchs.\n\n23. Sunday. Second [Sunday]. Fast-breaking [Eve] of the Arajavork [Precursors] Fast. And for the rest, see in the First Volume up to Vardavar [Transfiguration], keeping the order of this place.\n\nFebruary\n\n13. Sunday. Tone 8 [dk]. Great Lent [Bun Barekendan].\n\n14. Monday. Tone 1 [az / ad]. Presentation of the Lord [Tyarnndaraj]. See according to the order in the First Volume.\n\nApril\n\n3. Sunday. Tone 1 [adz / ad]. Easter [Zatik]: Day of the Resurrection of Christ.\n\n7. Thursday. Tone 5 [gch / g2]. Feast of the Annunciation of the Holy Virgin.",
